  "question": {
    "text": "A circular disc reaches from top to bottom of an inclined plane of length $l$. When it slips down the plane, if takes $t \\mathrm{~s}$. When it rolls down the plane then it takes $\\left(\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\right)^{1 / 2} t \\mathrm{~s}$, where $\\alpha$ is _________",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "For slipping\n$\\begin{aligned}& \\mathrm{a}=\\mathrm{g} \\sin \\theta \\\\\n& \\ell=\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{at}^2 \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{t}=\\sqrt{\\frac{2 \\ell}{\\mathrm{g} \\sin \\theta}}\\end{aligned}$\nFor rolling\n$\\begin{aligned}& \\mathrm{a}^{\\prime}=\\frac{\\mathrm{g} \\sin \\theta}{1+\\frac{\\mathrm{k}^2}{\\mathrm{R}^2}}\\left[\\mathrm{k}=\\frac{\\mathrm{R}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right] \\\\& \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{a}^{\\prime}=\\frac{2 \\mathrm{~g} \\sin \\theta}{3} \\\\& \\ell=\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{a}^{\\prime}\\left(\\mathrm{t}^{\\prime}\\right)^2 \\\\& \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{t}^{\\prime}=\\sqrt{\\frac{6 \\ell}{2 \\mathrm{~g} \\sin \\theta}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{\\alpha}{2}} \\sqrt{\\frac{2 \\ell}{\\mathrm{g} \\sin \\theta}} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\alpha=3\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
